{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>He who dwells in the shelter of Elyon</b> — it is possible that this psalm too is by Moses, or by one of the poets, and he says to the servant of HaShem: Hear me, you who dwell in the shelter of Elyon — which is HaShem." "And the word בסתר is in construct state, like בצל שדי יתלונן, for the meaning is doubled, as is the rule."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 91, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:51.469412835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}